# cloudflared's own env file (`cp cloudflared.env.example cloudflared.env`,
# `chmod 600 cloudflared.env`). Kept out of .env on purpose: the app
# container receives every .env variable, and the tunnel token lets whoever
# holds it run a connector for this tunnel.
#
# Cloudflare Tunnel token (Zero Trust dashboard -> Networks -> Tunnels -> your
# tunnel -> the "Docker" install command has it).
TUNNEL_TOKEN=
